$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">If&nbsp;(<span class="italic">x</span>, <span class="italic">y</span>) is a solution of the system of equations above and <span class="italic">x</span> &gt; 0, what is the value of&nbsp;<span class="italic">xy</span> ?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p>1</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p>2</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p>3</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p>9</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. Substituting <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_002_572bc813.png" alt="x squared"></span> for <span class="italic">y</span> in the second equation gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_003_3be06193.png" alt="2 times, x squared, plus 6, equals, 2 times, open parenthesis, x plus 3, close parenthesis"></span>. This equation can be solved as follows:<div class="tcp-03c15f24-799a-44a2-be34-df400508c3e3"><table class="table_Borderless tcp-c425e124-3227-4af9-a2c7-652aeb085881"><tbody><tr><td class="tcp-af3a9c03-4eb8-4c37-a5f8-e51ed84f3376"><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_004_6a358700.png" alt="2 x squared, plus 6, equals, 2 x plus 6"></span></td><td class="tcp-5ad91201-6479-447c-99f8-e1b070cc9dc9">Apply the distributive property.</td></tr><tr><td class="tcp-7d1d2c42-c52b-455a-aee9-f175160688c0"><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_005_c97e1a40.png" alt="2 x squared, plus 6, minus 2 x, minus 6, equals 0"></span></td><td class="tcp-9c78c3d0-df94-453c-8065-266e563e9e80">Subtract 2x and 6 from both sides of the equation.</td></tr><tr><td class="tcp-4e7eba3a-196e-4425-9f98-804573042022"><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_006_df558f19.png" alt="2 x squared, minus 2 x, equals 0"></span></td><td class="tcp-d1031b08-e2ba-45a9-af31-cfb869f1f2ef">Combine like terms.</td></tr><tr><td class="tcp-ef000b74-257c-4399-b576-122afdf9e904"><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_007_df2ea2d9.png" alt="2 x times, open parenthesis, x minus 1, close parenthesis, equals 0"></span></td><td class="tcp-d4bca920-a349-422d-9047-df707fdc8bc8">Factor both terms on the left side of the equation<br>by 2x.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Thus, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_008_3f34714f.png" alt="x equals 0"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_009_70a1cc99.png" alt="x equals 1"></span> are the solutions to the system. Since <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_010_8d906565.png" alt="x is greater than 0"></span>, only <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_011_70a1cc99.png" alt="x equals 1"></span> needs to be considered. The value of <span class="italic">y</span> when <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_012_70a1cc99.png" alt="x equals 1"></span> is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_013_26ca212f.png" alt="y equals x squared, which equals 1 squared, which equals 1"></span>. Therefore, the value of <span class="italic">xy</span> is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_014_b5d40299.png" alt="1 times 1, equals 1"></span>.</p><p>Choices B, C, and D are incorrect and likely result from a computational or conceptual error when solving this system of equations.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 15, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"876a731c","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"05314-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.B.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><table class=\"table_Borderless\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"para_center tcp-2d44842d-4280-4f9a-a0a3-e9e3d2b9384f\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_000_c90fecbf.png\" alt=\"y equals x squared\"></span></td></tr><tr><td class=\"para_center tcp-6955af12-df0e-4388-bd3b-8f1f084d1b32\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_001_2b4ef07f.png\" alt=\"2 y plus 6, equals, 2 times, open parenthesis, x plus 3, close\nparenthesis\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n","stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">If&nbsp;(<span class=\"italic\">x</span>, <span class=\"italic\">y</span>) is a solution of the system of equations above and <span class=\"italic\">x</span> &gt; 0, what is the value of&nbsp;<span class=\"italic\">xy</span> ?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p>1</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p>2</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p>3</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p>9</p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. Substituting <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_002_572bc813.png\" alt=\"x squared\"></span> for <span class=\"italic\">y</span> in the second equation gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_003_3be06193.png\" alt=\"2 times, x squared, plus 6, equals, 2 times, open parenthesis, x plus 3, close parenthesis\"></span>. This equation can be solved as follows:<div class=\"tcp-03c15f24-799a-44a2-be34-df400508c3e3\"><table class=\"table_Borderless tcp-c425e124-3227-4af9-a2c7-652aeb085881\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"tcp-af3a9c03-4eb8-4c37-a5f8-e51ed84f3376\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_004_6a358700.png\" alt=\"2 x squared, plus 6, equals, 2 x plus 6\"></span></td><td class=\"tcp-5ad91201-6479-447c-99f8-e1b070cc9dc9\">Apply the distributive property.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"tcp-7d1d2c42-c52b-455a-aee9-f175160688c0\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_005_c97e1a40.png\" alt=\"2 x squared, plus 6, minus 2 x, minus 6, equals 0\"></span></td><td class=\"tcp-9c78c3d0-df94-453c-8065-266e563e9e80\">Subtract 2x and 6 from both sides of the equation.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"tcp-4e7eba3a-196e-4425-9f98-804573042022\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_006_df558f19.png\" alt=\"2 x squared, minus 2 x, equals 0\"></span></td><td class=\"tcp-d1031b08-e2ba-45a9-af31-cfb869f1f2ef\">Combine like terms.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"tcp-ef000b74-257c-4399-b576-122afdf9e904\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_007_df2ea2d9.png\" alt=\"2 x times, open parenthesis, x minus 1, close parenthesis, equals 0\"></span></td><td class=\"tcp-d4bca920-a349-422d-9047-df707fdc8bc8\">Factor both terms on the left side of the equation<br>by 2x.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Thus, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_008_3f34714f.png\" alt=\"x equals 0\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_009_70a1cc99.png\" alt=\"x equals 1\"></span> are the solutions to the system. Since <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_010_8d906565.png\" alt=\"x is greater than 0\"></span>, only <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_011_70a1cc99.png\" alt=\"x equals 1\"></span> needs to be considered. The value of <span class=\"italic\">y</span> when <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_012_70a1cc99.png\" alt=\"x equals 1\"></span> is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_013_26ca212f.png\" alt=\"y equals x squared, which equals 1 squared, which equals 1\"></span>. Therefore, the value of <span class=\"italic\">xy</span> is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/876a731c/img_014_b5d40299.png\" alt=\"1 times 1, equals 1\"></span>.</p><p>Choices B, C, and D are incorrect and likely result from a computational or conceptual error when solving this system of equations.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":15,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959628,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"876a731c","skill_cd":"P.B.","score_band_range_cd":5,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","createDate":1691007959628,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"05314-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"c55b23b0-1cb1-4637-a1c6-e710dc6d07b0","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"05314-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><table class=\"table_Borderless\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"para_center tcp-2d44842d-4280-4f9a-a0a3-e9e3d2b9384f\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y equals x squared\"></span></td></tr><tr><td class=\"para_center tcp-6955af12-df0e-4388-bd3b-8f1f084d1b32\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 y plus 6, equals, 2 times, open parenthesis, x plus 3, close\nparenthesis\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">If&nbsp;(<span class=\"italic\">x</span>, <span class=\"italic\">y</span>) is a solution of the system of equations above and <span class=\"italic\">x</span> &gt; 0, what is the value of&nbsp;<span class=\"italic\">xy</span> ?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p>1</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p>2</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p>3</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p>9</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"a","rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. Substituting <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x squared\"></span> for <span class=\"italic\">y</span> in the second equation gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 times, x squared, plus 6, equals, 2 times, open parenthesis, x plus 3, close parenthesis\"></span>. This equation can be solved as follows:<div class=\"tcp-03c15f24-799a-44a2-be34-df400508c3e3\"><table class=\"table_Borderless tcp-c425e124-3227-4af9-a2c7-652aeb085881\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"tcp-af3a9c03-4eb8-4c37-a5f8-e51ed84f3376\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 x squared, plus 6, equals, 2 x plus 6\"></span></td><td class=\"tcp-5ad91201-6479-447c-99f8-e1b070cc9dc9\">Apply the distributive property.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"tcp-7d1d2c42-c52b-455a-aee9-f175160688c0\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 x squared, plus 6, minus 2 x, minus 6, equals 0\"></span></td><td class=\"tcp-9c78c3d0-df94-453c-8065-266e563e9e80\">Subtract 2x and 6 from both sides of the equation.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"tcp-4e7eba3a-196e-4425-9f98-804573042022\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 x squared, minus 2 x, equals 0\"></span></td><td class=\"tcp-d1031b08-e2ba-45a9-af31-cfb869f1f2ef\">Combine like terms.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"tcp-ef000b74-257c-4399-b576-122afdf9e904\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 x times, open parenthesis, x minus 1, close parenthesis, equals 0\"></span></td><td class=\"tcp-d4bca920-a349-422d-9047-df707fdc8bc8\">Factor both terms on the left side of the equation<br>by 2x.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Thus, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x equals 0\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x equals 1\"></span> are the solutions to the system. Since <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x is greater than 0\"></span>, only <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x equals 1\"></span> needs to be considered. The value of <span class=\"italic\">y</span> when <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x equals 1\"></span> is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y equals x squared, which equals 1 squared, which equals 1\"></span>. Therefore, the value of <span class=\"italic\">xy</span> is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"1 times 1, equals 1\"></span>.</p><p>Choices B, C, and D are incorrect and likely result from a computational or conceptual error when solving this system of equations.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959628,"updateDate":1691007959628}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959628, 1691007959628),
