</mrow>
</math></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">In the given equation, <math alttext="c"><mi>c</mi>
</math> is a constant. The equation has exactly one solution. What is the value of <math alttext="c"><mi>c</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"57a3f5f5-aa5d-4db6-b9c5-1c4c56499e47","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 68\"><mo>-</mo><mn>68</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"fbb2ee95-4a94-4d1c-a555-9a609334e769","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 50\"><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c418cc44-c63c-4e09-ac4f-bf249c658a8d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 32\"><mo>-</mo><mn>32</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f3589979-eb07-491b-a609-b33e98c363e8","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["fbb2ee95-4a94-4d1c-a555-9a609334e769"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. It's given that the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="minus 2 x squared plus 20 x plus c equals 0"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="c"><mi>c</mi></math> is a constant, has exactly one solution. A quadratic equation of the form <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a x squared plus b x plus c equals 0"><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> has exactly one solution if and only if its discriminant, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b squared minus 4 a c"><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></math>, is equal to zero. It follows that for the given equation, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a equals negative 2"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b equals 20"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 2"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a"><mi>a</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="20"><mn>20</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b"><mi>b</mi></math> in <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b squared minus 4 a c"><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="20 squared minus 4 left parenthesis negative 2 right parenthesis left parenthesis c right parenthesis"><msup><mn>20</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="400 plus 8 c"><mn>400</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>c</mi></math>. Since the discriminant must equal zero, it follows that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="400 plus 8 c equals 0"><mn>400</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="400"><mn>400</mn></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="8 c equals negative 400"><mn>8</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>400</mn></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="8"><mn>8</mn></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="c equals negative 50"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="c"><mi>c</mi></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 50"><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"88a0c425","external_id":"87a33c1a-0dd6-4c06-953e-5ebde0abb83e","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"4c6dfb25-d269-421c-bb9d-706b17949400","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.B.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"minus 2 x squared plus 20 x plus c equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t\t</msup>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>20</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>c</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the given equation, <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math> is a constant. The equation has exactly one solution. What is the value of <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"57a3f5f5-aa5d-4db6-b9c5-1c4c56499e47","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 68\"><mo>-</mo><mn>68</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"fbb2ee95-4a94-4d1c-a555-9a609334e769","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 50\"><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c418cc44-c63c-4e09-ac4f-bf249c658a8d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 32\"><mo>-</mo><mn>32</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f3589979-eb07-491b-a609-b33e98c363e8","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["fbb2ee95-4a94-4d1c-a555-9a609334e769"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. It's given that the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"minus 2 x squared plus 20 x plus c equals 0\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi></math> is a constant, has exactly one solution. A quadratic equation of the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a x squared plus b x plus c equals 0\"><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> has exactly one solution if and only if its discriminant, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b squared minus 4 a c\"><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></math>, is equal to zero. It follows that for the given equation, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a equals negative 2\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b equals 20\"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 2\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b squared minus 4 a c\"><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"20 squared minus 4 left parenthesis negative 2 right parenthesis left parenthesis c right parenthesis\"><msup><mn>20</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"400 plus 8 c\"><mn>400</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>c</mi></math>. Since the discriminant must equal zero, it follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"400 plus 8 c equals 0\"><mn>400</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"400\"><mn>400</mn></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8 c equals negative 400\"><mn>8</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>400</mn></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c equals negative 50\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 50\"><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1755117017720,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"88a0c425","skill_cd":"P.B.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","createDate":1755117017720,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"","external_id":"87a33c1a-0dd6-4c06-953e-5ebde0abb83e","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"4c6dfb25-d269-421c-bb9d-706b17949400","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"minus 2 x squared plus 20 x plus c equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t\t</msup>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>20</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>c</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the given equation, <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math> is a constant. The equation has exactly one solution. What is the value of <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math>?</p>","keys":["fbb2ee95-4a94-4d1c-a555-9a609334e769"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"57a3f5f5-aa5d-4db6-b9c5-1c4c56499e47","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 68\"><mo>-</mo><mn>68</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"fbb2ee95-4a94-4d1c-a555-9a609334e769","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 50\"><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c418cc44-c63c-4e09-ac4f-bf249c658a8d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 32\"><mo>-</mo><mn>32</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f3589979-eb07-491b-a609-b33e98c363e8","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. It's given that the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"minus 2 x squared plus 20 x plus c equals 0\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi></math> is a constant, has exactly one solution. A quadratic equation of the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a x squared plus b x plus c equals 0\"><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> has exactly one solution if and only if its discriminant, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b squared minus 4 a c\"><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></math>, is equal to zero. It follows that for the given equation, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a equals negative 2\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b equals 20\"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 2\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b squared minus 4 a c\"><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"20 squared minus 4 left parenthesis negative 2 right parenthesis left parenthesis c right parenthesis\"><msup><mn>20</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"400 plus 8 c\"><mn>400</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>c</mi></math>. Since the discriminant must equal zero, it follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"400 plus 8 c equals 0\"><mn>400</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"400\"><mn>400</mn></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8 c equals negative 400\"><mn>8</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>400</mn></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c equals negative 50\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 50\"><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"87a33c1a-0dd6-4c06-953e-5ebde0abb83e","correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1755117017720,"updateDate":1755117017720}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017720, 1755117017720),
