.504759 223.115522 \nL 94.550797 221.471859 \nL 99.176331 219.742474 \nL 103.801865 217.769082 \nL 108.006896 215.734467 \nL 112.211927 213.440471 \nL 115.996455 211.126857 \nL 119.780983 208.549405 \nL 123.565511 205.678029 \nL 126.929536 202.85193 \nL 130.293561 199.741103 \nL 133.657586 196.316862 \nL 137.021611 192.54763 \nL 139.965133 188.939312 \nL 142.908655 185.01483 \nL 145.852176 180.746483 \nL 148.795698 176.104141 \nL 151.73922 171.055033 \nL 154.682742 165.563519 \nL 157.626264 159.590835 \nL 160.569785 153.094821 \nL 163.513307 146.029621 \nL 166.456829 138.345364 \nL 169.400351 129.987808 \nL 172.343873 120.897956 \nL 175.287394 111.011646 \nL 178.230916 100.259091 \nL 181.174438 88.56439 \nL 184.11796 75.844991 \nL 187.061482 62.01111 \nL 190.005003 46.965095 \nL 192.107519 35.417347 \nL 192.107519 35.417347 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:2.3;\"></path>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"p424c901d6f\">\n   <rect height=\"260.82\" width=\"268.898496\" x=\"7.2\" y=\"7.2\"></rect>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for graph of a curve\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>Moving from left to right:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>The curve passes from quadrant 2 to quadrant 1.</li>\n<li>In quadrant 2, the curve trends up sharply to the point (0 comma 3).</li>\n<li>In quadrant 1, the curve trends up sharply.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>The curve passes through the following points:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>approximately (negative 1 comma 0.2)</li>\n<li>(0 comma 3)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The graph of the exponential function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> is shown, where <math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>. The <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["3"],"correct_answer":["3"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math>. For the graph of the exponential function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> shown, where <math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>, it's given that the <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. The graph intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at the point <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Therefore,&nbsp;the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1743430554982,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"893c7519","skill_cd":"P.C.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","createDate":1743430554982,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"","external_id":"56af9a6d-1c30-4ea5-a528-45b60f366d79","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"aaf18daa-cec9-4cd8-b781-d3b5298e941d","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"type":"spr","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"275.22pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 287.764248 275.22\" width=\"287.764248pt\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Graph of a curve in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis ranges from negative 1 to 1. The y axis ranges from negative 1 to 12. Refer to long descriptio